<title>JAPAN: Japan's Dec household spending down 0.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan's Dec household spending down 0.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's household spending in December fell 0.6 percent in real terms from a year earlier to an average 420,121 yen per household, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The agency said household spending fell 0.1 percent in real terms in calendar 1996.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of year-on-year percentage changes in real and nominal terms:</p>
<p>						Dec		   Nov</p>
<p>					 Real   Nominal    Real   Nominal</p>
<p> Overall household spending   -0.6     -0.1	+1.7    +2.0</p>
<p>(average 420,121 yen)  Spending by wage earners     -0.8     -0.3	+3.1    +3.4</p>
<p>(average 455,324 yen)</p>
</text>
